<edge id="R:23edaff13b" source="paper-B:Measurement:langmuir-qm-phenol-hargo-7-10-rgo-6-02-h" target="C:Metric:maximum-adsorption-capacity"><data key="e_predicate">MEASURED_BY</data><data key="e_source_id">paper-B</data><data key="e_strength">direct</data><data key="e_conditions">{}</data><data key="e_paragraph_id">p-0094</data><data key="e_quote">The maximum adsorption capacity calculated according to the Langmuir model was 7.10 mg/g for HA–rGO</data></edge>
<edge id="R:e40c01f0f8" source="paper-B:Measurement:langmuir-qm-phenol-hargo-7-10-rgo-6-02-h" target="paper-B:Condition:static-batch-25-c-phenol-0-515-mg-dm3-0"><data key="e_predicate">UNDER_CONDITION</data><data key="e_source_id">paper-B</data><data key="e_strength">direct</data><data key="e_conditions">{}</data><data key="e_paragraph_id">p-0028</data><data key="e_quote">The experiments were performed under static batch conditions at 25 °C using freshly prepared aqueous phenol solutions with initial concentrations ranging from 0.5 to 15 mg/dm3.</data></edge>
<edge id="R:aa2d423e03" source="paper-B:Sample:humic-acid-reduced-graphene-oxide-compos" target="paper-B:Sample:initial-humic-acid-sample-shubarkol-coal"><data key="e_predicate">OUTPERFORMS</data><data key="e_source_id">paper-B</data><data key="e_strength">direct</data><data key="e_conditions">{&quot;adsorbate&quot;: &quot;phenol&quot;, &quot;criterion&quot;: &quot;adsorption capacity&quot;, &quot;range&quot;: &quot;0.5–15 mg/dm3&quot;}</data><data key="e_paragraph_id">p-0089</data><data key="e_quote">the HA-rGO composite exhibited a higher adsorption capacity toward phenol than the initial humic acid and rGO</data></edge>
<edge id="R:7dbf743e4e" source="paper-B:Sample:humic-acid-reduced-graphene-oxide-compos" target="paper-B:Sample:rgo-sample-sigma-aldrich"><data key="e_predicate">OUTPERFORMS</data><data key="e_source_id">paper-B</data><data key="e_strength">direct</data><data key="e_conditions">{&quot;adsorbate&quot;: &quot;phenol&quot;, &quot;criterion&quot;: &quot;adsorption capacity&quot;, &quot;range&quot;: &quot;0.5–15 mg/dm3&quot;}</data><data key="e_paragraph_id">p-0089</data><data key="e_quote">the HA-rGO composite exhibited a higher adsorption capacity toward phenol than the initial humic acid and rGO</data></edge>
<edge id="R:baf9270632" source="C:Method:langmuir-isotherm-model" target="paper-B:Measurement:hargo-isotherm-fit-langmuir-r2-0-9804-vs"><data key="e_predicate">FITS</data><data key="e_source_id">paper-B</data><data key="e_strength">direct</data><data key="e_conditions">{}</data><data key="e_paragraph_id">p-0094</data><data key="e_quote">phenol adsorption on the HA–rGO composite was better described by the Langmuir model, with R2 = 0.9804</data></edge>
<edge id="R:2cb5c11409" source="C:Method:langmuir-isotherm-model" target="C:Method:freundlich-isotherm-model"><data key="e_predicate">OUTPERFORMS</data><data key="e_source_id">paper-B</data><data key="e_strength">direct</data><data key="e_conditions">{&quot;sample&quot;: &quot;HA–rGO composite&quot;, &quot;criterion&quot;: &quot;R2&quot;, &quot;adsorbate&quot;: &quot;phenol&quot;}</data><data key="e_paragraph_id">p-0094</data><data key="e_quote">phenol adsorption on the HA–rGO composite was better described by the Langmuir model, with R2 = 0.9804, whereas the Freundlich model gave R2 = 0.9515</data></edge>
<edge id="R:4082be4336" source="C:Method:freundlich-isotherm-model" target="C:Method:langmuir-isotherm-model"><data key="e_predicate">OUTPERFORMS</data><data key="e_source_id">paper-B</data><data key="e_strength">direct</data><data key="e_conditions">{&quot;sample&quot;: &quot;initial humic acid&quot;, &quot;criterion&quot;: &quot;R2&quot;, &quot;adsorbate&quot;: &quot;phenol&quot;}</data><data key="e_paragraph_id">p-0092</data><data key="e_quote">The adsorption of phenol on HA was better described by the Freundlich model</data></edge>
<edge id="R:22295aa5d1" source="C:Method:freundlich-isotherm-model" target="paper-B:Measurement:ha-isotherm-fit-freundlich-r2-0-9092-vs"><data key="e_predicate">FITS</data><data key="e_source_id">paper-B</data><data key="e_strength">direct</data><data key="e_conditions">{}</data><data key="e_paragraph_id">p-0092</data><data key="e_quote">for which the coefficient of determination was R2 = 0.9092, compared with R2 = 0.8502 for the Langmuir model</data></edge>
<edge id="R:73b58d054f" source="C:Method:langmuir-isotherm-model" target="C:Method:freundlich-isotherm-model"><data key="e_predicate">COMPARED_WITH</data><data key="e_source_id">paper-B</data><data key="e_strength">direct</data><data key="e_conditions">{&quot;sample&quot;: &quot;rGO&quot;, &quot;criterion&quot;: &quot;R2&quot;, &quot;adsorbate&quot;: &quot;phenol&quot;}</data><data key="e_paragraph_id">p-0093</data><data key="e_quote">neither model can be considered unambiguously predominant for rGO within the investigated concentration range</data></edge>
<edge id="R:b3fdf59987" source="paper-B:Sample:rgo-sample-sigma-aldrich" target="paper-B:Measurement:rgo-isotherm-fit-langmuir-r2-0-9266-vs-f"><data key="e_predicate">HAS_RESULT</data><data key="e_source_id">paper-B</data><data key="e_strength">direct</data><data key="e_conditions">{}</data><data key="e_paragraph_id">p-0093</data><data key="e_quote">For rGO, the Langmuir and Freundlich models showed comparable agreement with the experimental data</data></edge>
<edge id="R:bcdd4a6376" source="C:Method:pseudo-second-order-kinetic-model" target="paper-B:Measurement:hargo-kinetics-pso-r2-0-9939-vs-pfo-0-97"><data key="e_predicate">FITS</data><data key="e_source_id">paper-B</data><data key="e_strength">direct</data><data key="e_conditions">{&quot;C0&quot;: &quot;7.5 mg/dm3&quot;}</data><data key="e_paragraph_id">p-0098</data><data key="e_quote">The pseudo-second-order model also showed better agreement for the HA–rGO composite</data></edge>
